    "configuration": [
      {
        "title": "Setup",
        "properties": {
          "phren.mcpServerPath": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "order": 1,
            "markdownDescription": "Absolute path to the Phren MCP server entrypoint (`index.js`). Leave blank to auto-detect (checks MCP config, npx cache, and PATH)."
          },
          "phren.nodePath": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "node",
            "order": 2,
            "markdownDescription": "Path to the Node.js binary used to spawn the MCP server. VS Code's built-in Electron binary won't work — this must point to a real `node` install."
          },
          "phren.storePath": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "order": 3,
            "markdownDescription": "Path to the Phren store directory (where projects, findings, and config live). Leave blank to use `~/.phren`."
          },
          "phren.onboardingComplete": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false,
            "order": 4,
            "description": "Internal flag — set to true after first-run onboarding completes. Reset to false to re-trigger onboarding."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Capture Behavior",
        "properties": {
          "phren.findingSensitivity": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "minimal",
              "conservative",
              "balanced",
              "aggressive"
            ],
            "default": "balanced",
            "order": 1,
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "Minimal — Only save findings when you explicitly ask (e.g. 'remember this'). Zero auto-capture. Best for: users who want full manual control.",
              "Conservative — Save decisions and pitfalls only. Auto-capture up to 3 findings per session. Best for: small projects or when noise is a concern.",
              "Balanced — Save non-obvious patterns, decisions, pitfalls, and bugs worth remembering. Auto-capture up to 10 per session. Best for: most projects.",
              "Aggressive — Save everything worth remembering, err on the side of capturing. Auto-capture up to 20 per session. Best for: complex projects with many contributors."
            ],
            "markdownDescription": "**Master control for how aggressively Phren captures findings.** This sets the session cap (how many findings can be auto-captured per session) and the agent instruction (what kinds of insights to save). Higher levels capture more but may produce noise; lower levels are quieter but may miss useful patterns."
          },
          "phren.proactivity": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "high",
              "medium",
              "low"
            ],
            "default": "high",
            "order": 2,
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "High — Always auto-capture findings and tasks without waiting for explicit signals. Phren actively monitors conversations for insights worth saving.",
              "Medium — Only auto-capture when explicit signals are detected (e.g. words like 'add finding', 'worth remembering', tags like [decision], [pitfall]). Quieter but still responsive.",
              "Low — Never auto-capture. Phren only saves findings and tasks when you explicitly use a command or MCP tool. Fully manual."
            ],
            "markdownDescription": "**Global proactivity level** for both findings and tasks. Controls whether Phren auto-captures insights or waits for explicit signals. Override per-type with the findings and tasks settings below."
          },
          "phren.proactivityFindings": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "high",
              "medium",
              "low"
            ],
            "default": "high",
            "order": 3,
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "High — Always auto-capture findings (patterns, decisions, bugs) from conversations.",
              "Medium — Only capture findings when explicit signals detected (e.g. 'remember this', [decision] tags).",
              "Low — Never auto-capture findings. Only saved via explicit add_finding calls."
            ],
            "markdownDescription": "**Override proactivity for findings only.** When set, this takes priority over the global `#phren.proactivity#` for finding capture. Leave at the same level as global proactivity if you don't need a separate override."
          },
          "phren.proactivityTasks": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "high",
              "medium",
              "low"
            ],
            "default": "high",
            "order": 4,
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "High — Always auto-capture tasks from conversations (e.g. 'we should fix X' → task created).",
              "Medium — Only capture tasks when explicit signals detected (e.g. 'add this to tasks', 'put that on the todo list').",
              "Low — Never auto-capture tasks. Only created via explicit add_task calls."
            ],
            "markdownDescription": "**Override proactivity for tasks only.** When set, this takes priority over the global `#phren.proactivity#` for task capture. Leave at the same level as global proactivity if you don't need a separate override."
          },
          "phren.taskMode": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "off",
              "manual",
              "suggest",
              "auto"
            ],
            "default": "auto",
            "order": 5,
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "Off — Task system completely disabled. No task tracking, no task injection into context.",
              "Manual — Tasks only created when you explicitly request them (e.g. 'add task: fix the login bug').",
              "Suggest — Agent suggests tasks but waits for your confirmation before adding them. Good for reviewing before committing.",
              "Auto — Agent adds tasks automatically when it detects actionable work items in conversation. Most hands-off."
            ],
            "markdownDescription": "**Task automation mode.** Controls how the agent interacts with the task system. Separate from proactivity — this controls the agent's permission to create/manage tasks, while proactivity controls *when* it tries to."
          },
          "phren.autoExtract": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": true,
            "order": 6,
            "markdownDescription": "**Extract insights from project context on each prompt.** When enabled, the hook-prompt pipeline scans the current project for keywords and injects relevant phren findings into the agent's context. Disable if you want phren to be purely manual (search_knowledge only)."
          },
          "phren.autoCapture": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false,
            "order": 7,
            "markdownDescription": "**Extract insights from conversation transcripts at session end.** When enabled, phren analyzes the full conversation after a session ends and captures findings it missed during the session. Useful for catching patterns that only become apparent in retrospect. Requires an active LLM endpoint."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Hooks & Integration",
        "properties": {
          "phren.hooksEnabled": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": true,
            "order": 1,
            "markdownDescription": "**Master switch for phren hooks.** When disabled, no hooks fire on prompts, session starts, or stops — phren becomes a passive MCP server that only responds when explicitly called. Hooks handle: context injection (SessionStart), knowledge retrieval (UserPromptSubmit), and auto-save (Stop)."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Semantic Analysis (Offline)",
        "properties": {
          "phren.semanticDedup": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false,
            "order": 1,
            "markdownDescription": "**Semantic duplicate detection for offline maintenance.** Used by `phren maintain consolidate` and `phren maintain extract` when no agent session is active. Detects findings that say the same thing in different words and merges them.\n\n- **Live sessions**: Dedup uses the active agent (Claude/GPT) at no extra cost.\n- **Batch mode**: Uses a separate LLM call per finding group. Results cached 24h.\n- **Cost**: ~$0.01/batch-session with Haiku."
          },
          "phren.semanticConflict": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false,
            "order": 2,
            "markdownDescription": "**Semantic conflict detection for offline maintenance.** Used by `phren maintain consolidate` and `phren maintain extract` when no agent session is active. Detects findings that contradict each other (e.g. 'always use X' vs 'never use X') and annotates them.\n\n- **Live sessions**: Conflict detection uses the active agent at no extra cost.\n- **Batch mode**: Uses a separate LLM call per finding group. Results cached 24h.\n- **Cost**: ~$0.01/batch-session with Haiku."
          },
          "phren.llmModel": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "order": 3,
            "enum": [
              "",
              "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
              "claude-sonnet-4-6",
              "claude-opus-4-6",
              "gpt-4o-mini",
              "gpt-4o"
            ],
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "Server default (Haiku) — cheapest option, recommended",
              "Claude Haiku 4.5 — fast and cheap, best for batch operations (~$0.01/session)",
              "Claude Sonnet 4.6 — higher quality, ~10x more expensive than Haiku",
              "Claude Opus 4.6 — highest quality but very expensive for batch; not recommended",
              "GPT-4o mini — cost-effective OpenAI alternative for batch operations",
              "GPT-4o — expensive for batch operations; not recommended"
            ],
            "markdownDescription": "**LLM model for offline phren operations** (`consolidate`, `extract`). Only used when semantic dedup or conflict detection is enabled above.\n\n- **Live sessions**: The active agent handles dedup/conflict — this setting is ignored.\n- **Batch mode**: This model runs the analysis. Haiku is recommended for cost.\n- Sets the `PHREN_LLM_MODEL` environment variable."
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  },
